00:08:03,810 --> 00:08:05,490
我们不是追求完美。
Now, we're not shooting for perfection.

165
00:08:05,690 --> 00:08:08,824
我们追求的是比客户能看到的再深入一层。
We're shooting to go one level deeper than what your customer

166
00:08:08,824 --> 00:08:11,650
那种精细工艺会让他们感受到。
could see. That meticulous craft will show up for them.

167
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:15,356
而这种设计主张真正驱动标准和作品，
And this point of view really drives the standards

168
00:08:15,356 --> 00:08:18,571
尤其当有智能体参与、
and drives the work, especially when there's agents involved

169
00:08:18,571 --> 00:08:20,920
每天有更多事情发生时。
and so much more is happening on a daily basis.

170
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,000
那么如何培养它？
So how do you develop it?

171
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:26,880
坦率地说，关键在于变得非常擅长观察。
Frankly, it's all about getting really good at noticing.

172
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,549
观察你的用户需要什么、想要什么，
Notice what your users need and what

173
00:08:29,549 --> 00:08:31,480
而不只是他们说了什么。
they want, not just what they say.

174
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:35,566
观察你周围世界中哪些信号
Notice what about the world around you signals

175
00:08:35,566 --> 00:08:37,187
意味着“好”“很棒”和“一般”。
good and great and meh,

176
00:08:37,187 --> 00:08:41,537
要真正记录你使用的产品中的这些细节，
really take note of these things in the products that you use,

177
00:08:41,537 --> 00:08:44,010
但也要在类似情境中留意。
but also in analogous situations.

178
00:08:44,210 --> 00:08:46,413
这样你就能从艺术、科学和更广阔的视角中获得灵感，
So you can be inspired by art, science

179
00:08:46,413 --> 00:08:49,610
用于你创作的作品。
and a broader point of view in the work that you create.

180
00:08:50,010 --> 00:08:51,579
培养你的品味，
Building your sense of taste

181
00:08:51,579 --> 00:08:54,129
加深对周围世界的理解，
and your understanding of the world around you

182
00:08:54,129 --> 00:08:55,502
形成对什么是好、什么是出色的判断，
and what's good and great

183
00:08:55,502 --> 00:08:57,595
能真正提升你自己的标准，
can really improve your own standards

184
00:08:57,595 --> 00:08:59,360
而这些标准随后需要被规模化。
that you will then need to scale.

185
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,867
这就引出了我的第二条建议：
Which brings me to my second recommendation,

186
00:09:02,867 --> 00:09:05,690
把你的标准编码到机器里。
which is encode your standards into the machine.

187
00:09:06,530 --> 00:09:09,385
如果每个人都能有共同的理解
It'd be a wonderful world if every human had the shared

188
00:09:09,385 --> 00:09:12,050
并做出同样的决定，世界会很美好。
understandings and could make the same decision.

189
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:14,441
但现实是，人类未来不会参与
But the reality is, humans are not going

190
00:09:14,441 --> 00:09:16,930
所有这些决定。
to be a part of all of these decisions going forward.

191
00:09:17,730 --> 00:09:19,430
我们已经看到在没有设计师
We are seeing interfaces built

192
00:09:19,430 --> 00:09:21,130
在场的情况下构建出的界面。
without a designer in the room.

193
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:25,514
我们看到智能体在我们睡觉时发现问题并修复；
We're seeing agents finding problems and fixing them

194
00:09:25,514 --> 00:09:28,357
我们当然也看到 generative
while we sleep, and we're certainly seeing

195
00:09:28,357 --> 00:09:31,200
UI（生成式界面）为用户实时生成。
generative UI built in real time for users.

196
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:35,720
这就是为什么设计系统再次迎来高光时刻。
This is why design systems are having a moment again.

197
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,609
而过去的系统
And the system of yesterday

198
00:09:37,609 --> 00:09:39,680
和今天的系统不同。
is different than the system of today.

199
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:42,983
过去你不必把所有东西都写下来，
In the past, you didn't have to write everything down

200
00:09:42,983 --> 00:09:44,771
因为总有一位设计师
because there was always a designer

201
00:09:44,771 --> 00:09:46,380
在场来填补空白。
in the room to fill in the blanks.

202
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:50,115
现在我们必须支持分布式
Now we must enable distributed building

203
00:09:50,115 --> 00:09:52,020
构建和智能体式建造。
and agentic construction.

204
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:55,780
并且决策需要更容易被定义。
And the decisions need to be easier to define.

205
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:59,620
所以设计的对象不再是屏幕。
So the object of design is no longer the screen.

206
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,100
而是系统本身。
It is the system itself.

207
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:04,390
大家知道 Gutenberg（古腾堡）
Now, everybody knows Gutenberg

208
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:06,420
发明了第一台印刷机。
created the first printing press.

209
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:09,342
这个故事中较少为人知的部分，
The lesser known part of the story

210
00:10:09,342 --> 00:10:11,620
是他围绕印刷机构建的系统。
is the system he built around it.

211
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:15,149
他并不是只创造了 26
He didn't create just 26 lower case

212
00:10:15,149 --> 00:10:17,220
个小写字母和 26 个大写字母。
and 26 upper case letters.

213
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:20,956
他创造了 290 个独特字符，
He created 290 unique characters,

214
00:10:20,956 --> 00:10:25,060
包含不同宽度、缩写和连字。
different widths, abbreviations, ligatures.

215
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:28,221
他这样做的原因是，
And the reason that he did this is because

216
00:10:28,221 --> 00:10:31,241
在排版并希望两端对齐时，
when he typeset it and wanted it to be fully justified,

217
00:10:31,241 --> 00:10:33,723
他想确保不会出现
he wanted to make sure that there wouldn't be

218
00:10:33,723 --> 00:10:36,005
那种像河流和湖泊一样的怪异空白，
the weird rivers and lakes of white space

219
00:10:36,005 --> 00:10:38,420
以免破坏成品美感。
that erode the beauty of the final product.

220
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:41,656
本质上，他让它既具备可扩展性，
Essentially, he was making it both extensible

221
00:10:41,656 --> 00:10:45,170
又有足够明确的主张，使它在机器制造的同时，
and opinionated enough that it could feel as good as handmade,

222
00:10:45,170 --> 00:10:46,860
感觉能像手工制作一样好。
although it was machine made.

223
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:49,500
这也应该是我们追求的目标。
This is what we should be aiming for as well.

224
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:53,612
旧系统规模化的是“一致性”，
Now the old system scaled consistency,

225
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:56,880
但新系统需要规模化“设计意图”。
but the new system needs to scale intent.

226
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:59,368
我们在 Stripe 推进这件事时，
We've been working on this at Stripe

227
00:10:59,368 --> 00:11:01,360
一路上也遇到了一些障碍。
and have hit a few snags along the way.

228
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,760
所以我们还在摸索中。
And so we're figuring it out.

229
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:05,348
但我们想做的一件事，
But one of the things we want to do

230
00:11:05,348 --> 00:11:07,526
是让构建者几乎能瞬间
is we want to empower builders to go

231
00:11:07,526 --> 00:11:10,831
从提示词走向生产环境。
from prompt to production nearly instantaneously.

232
00:11:10,831 --> 00:11:12,858
和很多人一样，我们最初用 MCP（模型上下文协议），
Like many, we started with an MCP

233
00:11:12,858 --> 00:11:15,637
让它读取我们的设计文档，
that understood our design documentation,

234
00:11:15,637 --> 00:11:17,590
但结果并不理想。
but the results were not great.

235
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:19,538
它不够具体，
It wasn't specific enough,

236
00:11:19,538 --> 00:11:21,710
也没有驱动出正确的结果。
and it wasn't driving the right outcomes.

237
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:25,029
三个不同的人输入同一条提示词，
Three different people could put in the same prompt

238
00:11:25,029 --> 00:11:26,670
会得到三种不同的结果。
and get three different results.

239
00:11:27,670 --> 00:11:29,713
因此从那以后我们不断演进，现在创建了一个建立
So since then, we've evolved, and now

240
00:11:29,713 --> 00:11:32,350
在我们设计系统之上的 CLI（命令行工具）。
we have created a CLI built on our design system.

241
00:11:32,990 --> 00:11:33,990
它形成了一个执行框架（harness），
It makes a harness

242
00:11:33,990 --> 00:11:35,990
让 AI 变得顺从得多。
that makes the AI far more obedient.

243
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:39,054
现在它就在构建者们实际构建的地方，
Now it's where the builders are building

244
00:11:39,054 --> 00:11:42,410
并在正确的时间和位置读取文档，
and it consumes the documentation at the right time

245
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,440
以避免上下文退化（context rot）。
and place to avoid context rot.

246
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:48,756
重要的是，这个版本
Now, importantly, the big difference between this version

247
00:11:48,756 --> 00:11:50,543
和以往设计系统之间最大的区别在于，
and a previous design system is

248
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:53,017
它不只是组件和原子部件，
it's not just components and atomic parts,

249
00:11:53,017 --> 00:11:55,560
而是完整的模板和流程。
but it's actually full templates and flows.

250
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:59,276
所以系统实际上知道我们的产品应该如何表现，
So the system actually knows what our product is supposed

251
00:11:59,276 --> 00:12:02,580
以及所有部分如何组合在一起。
to behave like and how it all comes together, essentially.

252
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:05,340
它比过去更有明确的设计主张。
It's far more opinionated than it's been in the past.

253
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:09,301
我们把这些标准嵌入到生产方式中，
We embed these standards into the means of production,

254
00:12:09,301 --> 00:12:11,540
从而带来更连贯的产品。
which enables a more coherent product.

255
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:14,140
但这只是基线。
But this is just the baseline.

256
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:17,279
Christopher Alexander（建筑与设计思想家）说过，
Christopher Alexander said,

257
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:20,820
一个系统可以满足每一条规则，却仍然是“死”的。
"A system can satisfy every rule and still be dead."

258
00:12:21,410 --> 00:12:25,438
这就引出了我的第三条建议：
This brings me to my third recommendation,

259
00:12:25,438 --> 00:12:28,570
拒绝把“做完”和“做好”混为一谈。
refuse to confuse done with good.

260
00:12:30,010 --> 00:12:31,730
那道过滤器已经消失了。
The filter is gone.

261
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:35,280
过去，质量过滤机制基本上内建
It used to be the quality filter was essentially built

262
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:38,430
在产品开发流程的每个阶段，
into every stage of the product development process,

263
00:12:38,430 --> 00:12:40,250
甚至在项目开始之前就存在。
even before a project started.

264
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:45,050
我们有 20 个想法，却只能给其中一个配团队。
We've got 20 ideas and we can only staff one.

265
00:12:45,810 --> 00:12:49,522
然后我们一路上反复推敲、调整和修剪，
And then we poked and we prodded and we pruned along the way,

266
00:12:49,522 --> 00:12:52,250
产品成长得比较有条理。
and products grew somewhat methodically.

267
00:12:53,530 --> 00:12:56,530
而现在，我们一周就能把 20 个想法都做出来。
Well, now we can build 20 ideas in a week.

268
00:12:57,450 --> 00:12:59,250
这在很多方面都很棒。
This is awesome in many ways.

269
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:02,576
我们终于可以跳过讨论假设产品的理论会议，
And we can finally skip theoretical meetings talking about

270
00:13:02,576 --> 00:13:05,890
直接对手中真实的东西做出反应。
hypothetical products and react to the real thing in our hands.

271
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:10,478
过去贯穿全流程的质量筛选，
The filtering that used to be throughout the process

272
00:13:10,478 --> 00:13:12,686
现在得放到产品做出来之后；
now needs to happen post-build,

273
00:13:12,686 --> 00:13:14,812
这时再说“不”要难得多。
when it is a lot harder to say no.

274
00:13:14,812 --> 00:13:17,756
这正是“编辑”式把关者发挥作用的地方。
This is where the role of an editor comes in.

275
00:13:17,756 --> 00:13:20,781
如今，这个角色极其重要：
And it is ultra important in this day and age:

276
00:13:20,781 --> 00:13:23,480
你的团队里由谁负责这件事？
who is doing this in your organization?

277
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:26,496
谁在端到端地审视，
Who's looking at the end to end and understanding whether

278
00:13:26,496 --> 00:13:28,240
并理解我们是否真的在构建一个整体。
or not we're actually building a whole.

279
00:13:29,090 --> 00:13:32,050
这是我们必须戒除的一种新行为。
It's a new behavior we have to unlearn.

280
00:13:32,530 --> 00:13:36,610
也就是把“做出来”当成“做完”，把“做完”当成“做好”。
That built means done, and that done means good.

281
00:13:37,210 --> 00:13:39,938
对于任何正在磨练把关能力的人，
The most important thing I can say to anybody

282
00:13:39,938 --> 00:13:42,297
我能说的最重要的一点是：
working on their editing skills is you

283
00:13:42,297 --> 00:13:44,730
你必须像用户一样去体验它。
have to experience it like a user would.

284
00:13:45,890 --> 00:13:47,610
它真的解决问题了吗？
Does it actually solve the problem?

285
00:13:48,050 --> 00:13:49,774
它真的贴合用户
Is it actually attuned to the way

286
00:13:49,774 --> 00:13:51,370
思考问题的方式吗？
the user thinks about things?

287
00:13:52,190 --> 00:13:53,790
它真的连贯吗？
Is it actually coherent?

288
00:13:54,510 --> 00:13:56,270
很多东西单独看都很好。
A lot of things look good in isolation.

289
00:13:56,350 --> 00:13:59,259
但当你把这一切串到用户旅程里时，
But then when you pull it all together into the user journey,

290
00:13:59,259 --> 00:14:00,830
就会觉得有点脱节。
it feels a little disconnected.

291
00:14:01,990 --> 00:14:04,429
而且这不只是说“是”
And it's not just about saying yes or no,

292
00:14:04,429 --> 00:14:06,350
或“否”、“这个好”或“这个不该上”。
this is good or it shouldn't go.

293
00:14:06,830 --> 00:14:09,371
实际上是问：它真的完整成型了吗？
It's actually about: Is it even fully formed?

294
00:14:09,371 --> 00:14:11,310
我们怎么把它推向真正完整？
How can we push this to completion?

295
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:14,820
我们不希望“做完”成为“做好”的敌人。
We don't want done to be the enemy of good.

296
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:17,583
Nabil Qureshi（文章作者）写的一篇非常
A very insightful article by Nabil

297
00:14:17,583 --> 00:14:20,580
有洞见的文章谈到了什么让艺术伟大。
Qureshi talks about what makes art great.

298
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:23,447
他说这关乎意想不到的细节，
And he says it's about the unexpected details,

299
00:14:23,447 --> 00:14:25,578
那些让你觉得“哇，
those little surprising things you're like,

300
00:14:25,578 --> 00:14:27,540
真没想到他们连这个都想到了”的小惊喜。
wow, I can't believe they thought of that.

301
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:31,172
然后是表面之下的深层意义，
And then the deeper meaning that sits behind the surface

302
00:14:31,172 --> 00:14:34,526
或是把所有内容联结成一个整体的连贯主题；
or the continuous themes that tie it all together to a whole,

303
00:14:34,526 --> 00:14:36,940
这些正是 AI 不擅长的事情。
these are the things that AI is not great at.

304
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:40,939
但了解 AI 的不足在哪里，
But knowing what the gaps are in AI helps us

305
00:14:40,939 --> 00:14:44,310
能帮助我们更好地应对并填补这些空白。
better navigate that and fill these gaps in.

306
00:14:45,190 --> 00:14:49,074
正如 Nabil 所说，AI 粗制滥造的内容（slop）最
As Nabil says, one of the things that so offends us about

307
00:14:49,074 --> 00:14:52,790
让我们反感的一点，是那种“细节无关紧要”的感觉。
AI's slop is the sense that the details don't matter.

308
00:14:53,950 --> 00:14:56,950
杯子是绿色的，但就算是蓝色也没什么差别。
The cup is green, but may as well have been blue.

309
00:14:57,630 --> 00:15:01,596
把关者（editor）对每一个决策负责，
An editor takes accountability for every decision,

310
00:15:01,596 --> 00:15:04,120
这在很多情况下意味着每一个像素。
which is in many ways every pixel.

311
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:07,320
我给大家举个本次活动中的例子。
I'll give you an example from this event.

312
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:10,680
我的团队很荣幸负责设计这次活动。
So my team had the pleasure of designing the event.

313
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:14,400
Stefan 负责了这段精彩的开场动画。
Stefan worked on this fabulous opening animation.

314
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:18,704
他和团队先建了场景的 3D 模型，
He and the team started with a 3D model of the scene

315
00:15:18,704 --> 00:15:20,773
然后把模型导入 AI，
and then they brought it into AI

316
00:15:20,773 --> 00:15:23,400
用它辅助制作各种动画。
to help with the different animations.

317
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:26,020
这是第一个版本。
Now here's the first version.

318
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:28,260
很酷。
It's cool.

319
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:31,220
看到里面各种小部件很有趣。
It's fun to see the different little parts of it.

320
00:15:31,220 --> 00:15:32,740
它的运动方式也很不错。
And it's nice the way it moves.

321
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:36,003
但如果你逐像素仔细看，
But if you scrutinize it pixel by pixel,

322
00:15:36,003 --> 00:15:37,940
会感觉有点不对劲，对吧？
something feels off, right?

323
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:39,180
那不太像它应有的运动方式。
That's not quite the way it should move.

324
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:40,468
它有点抖动，
It's a little jittery

325
00:15:40,468 --> 00:15:42,964
而且你会想看到更多场景。
and you kind of want to get more of the scene.

326
00:15:42,964 --> 00:15:44,420
对，所以他又做了一次。
Right. So he did it again.

327
00:15:46,290 --> 00:15:51,763
一次又一次，在 56 次迭代之后，
And again and again, 56 iterations later,

